            <ArticleTitle>Providing sustainable catalytic solutions for a rapidly changing world: a summary and recommendations for urgent future action.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">20170068</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1098/rsta.2017.0068</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In addition to summarizing the main thrusts of each paper presented at this Discussion, other urgent issues involving the role (and characterization) of new catalysts for eliminating oxides of nitrogen, for using CO2 liberated from steel mills, for fuel cells and the need for rapid decarbonization of fossil fuels are outlined.This article is part of a discussion meeting issue 'Providing sustainable catalytic solutions for a rapidly changing world'.</AbstractText>
